<title>AUSTRIA: Buba's Welteke says sustainable budgets key to EMU.</title>
<headline>Buba's Welteke says sustainable budgets key to EMU.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Wednesday the 3.0 percent deficit criteria for Europe's single currency was not written in stone and that sustained low deficits were more important.</p>
<p>&quot;There is nothing about 3.0 percent in the Maastricht treaty,&quot; he told reporters as he arrived for a conference organised by the Austrian central bank.</p>
<p>Asked whether he believed if a sustainable budget deficit was more important than hitting the three percent, he replied: &quot;Yes.&quot; -- Vienna newsroom, +431 53112 274</p>
